Found while fixing the karr #11 follow-ups (static %DEFAULT_RESOURCE_MAP + class_namespaces in the qualified branch). Deliberately NOT fixed there, because both were flagged as pre-existing intentional decisions.

Both Kinds ship a class for a second api_version that has no qualified key in %DEFAULT_RESOURCE_MAP, so inflate() silently hands back the wrong schema version:

  events.k8s.io/v1        Event                   -> IO::K8s::Api::Core::V1::Event
                                                     (shipped: IO::K8s::Api::Events::V1::Event)
  autoscaling/v1          HorizontalPodAutoscaler -> IO::K8s::Api::Autoscaling::V2::HorizontalPodAutoscaler
                                                     (shipped: IO::K8s::Api::Autoscaling::V1::HorizontalPodAutoscaler)

The HPA one has teeth: autoscaling/v1 HPAs are common, and v1 spec carries
targetCPUUtilizationPercentage, which the V2 class does not declare -- so a real
autoscaling/v1 payload either loses that field or fails the constructor.

The decision to make is only about the QUALIFIED keys. Adding

  \x27events.k8s.io/v1/Event\x27                 => \x27Api::Events::V1::Event\x27,
  \x27autoscaling/v1/HorizontalPodAutoscaler\x27 => \x27Api::Autoscaling::V1::HorizontalPodAutoscaler\x27,

leaves both SHORT names exactly where they are (Event -> Core::V1, HPA -> V2), which
is the part that was called a settled decision. It only changes what
inflate()/expand_class($kind, $api_version) return when the caller explicitly
names that apiVersion.

Counter-argument for leaving it: it is a behaviour change for two widely used
Kinds in a release that already changes dispatch, and someone may be relying on
"an autoscaling/v1 HPA comes back as the V2 class".

Every other shipped core Kind now has a qualified key for every shipped version;
these two are the only remaining exceptions.
Resolved in 853a4c0: added events.k8s.io/v1/Event and autoscaling/v1/HorizontalPodAutoscaler qualified routes, bare-name defaults preserved (Core v1 Event, Autoscaling v2 HPA). Covered by t/43_spec_kind_dispatch.t (98 GVKs, all 14 collisions).
